                <p>{answer}</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    );
};

const FAQPage = () => {
    const faqData = [
        {
            question: "Why do cats purr?",
            answer: "While purring often indicates contentment, cats also purr to self-soothe when stressed or in pain. The frequency of a cat's purr has even been shown to help improve bone density and promote healing!"
        },
        {
            question: "Why do cats like boxes?",
            answer: "Boxes provide a sense of security and safety. In the wild, cats are both predators and prey, so having a confined space with only one opening helps them feel protected from potential threats."
        },
        {
            question: "Do cats always land on their feet?",
            answer: "Not always, but they have a \"righting reflex\" that allows them to twist their bodies in mid-air. Their flexible spine and lack of a collarbone help them reorient themselves quickly during a fall."
        },
        {
            question: "Why do cats have whiskers?",
            answer: "Whiskers are highly sensitive tactile organs called vibrissae. They help cats navigate in the dark, detect changes in air currents, and determine if they can fit through tight spaces."
        },
        {
            question: "Why do cats \"knead\" or \"make biscuits\"?",
            answer: "This behavior starts in kittenhood when they knead their mothers to stimulate milk flow. In adulthood, it's often a sign of comfort, affection, or a way to mark their territory with scent glands in their paws."
        }
    ];

    return (
        <main id="maincontent">
            <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
            {faqData.map((item, index) => (
                <FAQItem key={index} question={item.question} answer={item.answer} />
            ))}
        </main>
    );
};

const root = ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root'));
root.render(<FAQPage />);
